# Shared production baseline, committed. Public, non-sensitive values only —
# anything sensitive belongs in .env.local, which the deploy materializes on
# the host from GitHub Environment secrets and which overrides this file.
#
# Loaded two ways, and both have to stay true for a value here to take effect:
# varlock reads it when ENV=production, and docker/compose/prod.yaml lists it
# in env_file ahead of .env.local (the container runs no varlock).
#
# Production only. deploy-coolify.yml skips this file when IS_STAGING is set —
# staging supplies its own values through its GitHub Environment, or does
# without. It hardcodes ENV=production for both, so the name is the only thing
# keeping the two apart.

# PostHog analytics (Prologue). Public project key — the browser receives it
# in every page, so it is not a secret. POSTHOG_HOST and POSTHOG_ASSETS_HOST are
# omitted deliberately: .env.schema already defaults both to the EU endpoints.
POSTHOG_API_KEY=phc_CpBrrTFfWdX9GY7ZkYXdDhm4QmSV3oFTF9YtSs9AyiZZ
